<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The graphical representation of the zeros of <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{i}(G,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{i}(G,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is shown in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ item 2 ‣ 2 Independent domination polynomial of zero divisor graphs of commutative rings ‣ A note on the Independent domination polynomial of zero divisor graph of rings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (right), where green dots represent the zeros.</p>
