<div id="S2.I5.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n=p^{2m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n=p^{2m},</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is prime and </span><math id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a positive integer, then the independent domination polynomial of </span><math id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I5.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is given by</span></p>
