<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.2" class="ltx_p">All the exponents of the above polynomial are odd except last exponent which is even. So, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\leq\eta(D_{i}(G,x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\leq\eta(D_{i}(G,x))</annotation></semantics></math> and it follows that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{i}(G,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{i}(G,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is not unimodal. In fact <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta(D_{i}(G,x))=m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta(D_{i}(G,x))=m+1</annotation></semantics></math> as all the coefficients of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{1+p^{2m}-p^{2m-(i-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{1+p^{2m}-p^{2m-(i-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly increasing, for <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i=1,2,\dots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i=1,2,\dots,m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi(p^{2m})+\phi(p^{2m-1})+\dots+\phi(p^{m+1})=p^{2m}-p^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi(p^{2m})+\phi(p^{2m-1})+\dots+\phi(p^{m+1})=p^{2m}-p^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly greater than <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1+p^{2m}-p^{2m-(i-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1+p^{2m}-p^{2m-(i-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i=1,2,\dots,m." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i=1,2,\dots,m.</annotation></semantics></math> So the coefficients of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{i}(G,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{i}(G,x)</annotation></semantics></math> increase precisely <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m+1</annotation></semantics></math> times.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n=p^{2m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n=p^{2m},</annotation></semantics></math> the independent domination polynomial of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G\cong\Gamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G\cong\Gamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> in standard form is</p>
